  "problem": "Use the first three terms of the binomial expansion of $(2+x)^{9}$ in ascending powers of $x$ to approximate $(2.13)^{9}.$ Round your answer to three decimal places.\n\n$(2.13)^{9}\u2248$ \n{{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "The binomial theorem for positive integer $n$ states that\n\n$$\n(a+b)^{n}=(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{0}){a}^{n}{b}^{0}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{1}){a}^{n-1}{b}^{1}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{2}){a}^{n-2}{b}^{2}+\u2026+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{n}{n}){a}^{0}{b}^{n}.\n$$\n\nBy substituting $a=2,$ $b=x,$ and $n=9,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2+x)^{9} & =(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{9}{0})(2)^{9}(x)^{0}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{9}{1})(2)^{9-1}(x)^{1}+(\\genfrac{}{}{0pt}{}{9}{2})(2)^{9-2}(x)^{2}+\u22ef \\\\  & =1(2)^{9}+9(2)^{8}(x)^{1}+36(2)^{7}(x)^{2}+\u22ef \\\\  & =512+9(256)x+36(128){x}^{2}+\u22ef \\\\  & =512+2\\,304x+4\\,608{x}^{2}+\u22ef\\,.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, for small $x,$ we have\n\n$$\n(2+x)^{9}\u2248512+2\\,304x+4\\,608{x}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFinally, we substitute $x=0.13$ into the expansion of $(2+x)^{9}:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(2.13)^{9} & =(2+0.13)^{9} \\\\  & \u2248512+2\\,304(0.13)+4\\,608(0.13)^{2} \\\\  & =512+2\\,304(0.13)+4\\,608(0.016\\,9) \\\\  & =512+299.52+77.875\\,2 \\\\  & \u2248889.395,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nrounded to three decimal places.",
